speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, further to the announcement of the Minister of Finance (Mr. Wilson) I wish to advise that there have been discussions among the Parties. I believe you will find unanimous consent for the introduction and passage of the following motion. I move:
That, notwithstanding any standing or special order of the House, at 4.30 p.m. on Wednesday, February 18, 1987, the Speaker shall interrupt any proceedings then underway and proceed forthwith to the consideration of Ways and Means proceedings No. 10, for the purpose of the Budget statement of the Minister of Finance;
and that the House shall not adjourn until the adjournment of the debate on Ways and Means proceedings No. 10, following which Mr. Speaker shall adjourn the House until the next sitting day.
